in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{x}^{2}yz) \\\\  & =0+2 x^{2} y+4 x^{2} y \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=2}^{x=3}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=2}\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(27-8)\\cdot (4-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =114.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7866416-74af-5891-b8c9-f6c1a3a751ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3324145e-7687-5d49-96a6-669054ec659f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "560" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560066} {:answer/id #uuid "47e66ac9-ee46-5c7a-8e67-1eb9e32c798a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1680" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560072} {:answer/id #uuid "5ccd7816-11a4-5bce-9d80-c8d67c51a34e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560080} {:answer/id #uuid "749a79f0-6e45-50da-938f-c51698f56e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1680" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560084} {:answer/id #uuid "ab9b93a4-f2e3-5271-a9ea-41397d389507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "840" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "749a79f0-6e45-50da-938f-c51698f56e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1680" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560084} :answer-field/id #uuid "97a800ab-9ed7-5211-b33b-dbc03e4af6ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "57bd4c96-69f4-548a-a5d1-44f3f174d1f7" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=2$, $x=4$, $y=1$, $y=4$, $z=0$, $z=2$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F={e}^{z}\\,i+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+4{x}^{2}yz\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{x}^{2}yz) \\\\  & =0+2 x^{2} y+4 x^{2} y \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{4}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=2}^{x=4}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=4}\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(64-8)\\cdot (16-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1680.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7866416-74af-5891-b8c9-f6c1a3a751ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fbd81a5-13b8-5ffe-9128-1f49c13c0de3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560059} {:answer/id #uuid "b371c1c0-9316-5576-9287-dda41e7e9011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560093} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e50b77-a27d-5716-ab8f-aebb761a2186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560096} {:answer/id #uuid "ca848204-1be2-5069-9e32-ed8d35b33b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560106} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b4e512-f49c-5fe5-918b-c26f5ec9835f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9b4e512-f49c-5fe5-918b-c26f5ec9835f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560123} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e98cec3-2eff-5a26-95ad-fd16d5b3952a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5bdf8fdf-571c-520c-b00a-a7967e0d0e35" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=1$, $x=2$, $y=1$, $y=2$, $z=0$, $z=2$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F={e}^{z}\\,i+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+4{x}^{2}yz\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{x}^{2}yz) \\\\  & =0+2 x^{2} y+4 x^{2} y \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=1}^{x=2}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=2}\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(8-1)\\cdot (4-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7866416-74af-5891-b8c9-f6c1a3a751ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "133fe0f6-3b54-5025-8f85-59b3f508b498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560060} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab8ebf9-29b9-57ad-9537-957e82e6e2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560064} {:answer/id #uuid "45e66bb7-f2af-5ce9-91d0-f2364b6fe2d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560070} {:answer/id #uuid "e1636939-8a89-5eda-ae40-2c56066069d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560111} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ec6b0a-dfa5-5db6-9637-5aed73fbe309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8ec6b0a-dfa5-5db6-9637-5aed73fbe309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560115} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c27ed1e-c805-56df-b90b-eaa5a3199381" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2b380bb-5ecc-5211-8e29-58e3ad2580e7" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0$, $x=4$, $y=0$, $y=3$, $z=0$, $z=2$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=(3x+1)\\,i+3z\\,j+xy\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x + 1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =3+0+0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}3\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}3\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[3x]_{x=0}^{x=4}\\cdot (3-0)\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(12-0)\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7866416-74af-5891-b8c9-f6c1a3a751ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c942fa1-574a-5714-9d2d-2c69b9d82fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560074} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c805b0-0b04-5961-a32c-3e6aac097806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560095} {:answer/id #uuid "bec237d8-4f29-5dbe-bed4-f2b85d551520" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560099} {:answer/id #uuid "d296efa3-d724-5a7c-9971-af1e70d02d75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560107} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb39253-2ae7-5e79-bf75-158e82e1104c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bec237d8-4f29-5dbe-bed4-f2b85d551520" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560099} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5c52282-8c13-5e43-82c0-823fefb3d635" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c13ae8c6-2315-541d-82be-ca008e9a369b" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0$, $x=2$, $y=0$, $y=3$, $z=0$, $z=5$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=(2x+1)\\,i+3z\\,j+xy\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =2+0+0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{5}2\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{5}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[2x]_{x=0}^{x=2}\\cdot (3-0)\\cdot (5-0) \\\\  & =(4-0)\\cdot 3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7866416-74af-5891-b8c9-f6c1a3a751ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d11677f-b41e-53c2-82d6-2e3f223790cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{416}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560067} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc3bf00-f3c4-575c-be10-687ff969f6c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "416" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560083} {:answer/id #uuid "8d61fe98-57f2-508d-8d4a-f1a0ccc16cd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{208}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560088} {:answer/id #uuid "db42b8fd-128f-574b-a418-bc6e345e7388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-416" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560110} {:answer/id #uuid "e308e49f-0fb4-5ca5-9e0e-32529b1c5871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "208" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cc3bf00-f3c4-575c-be10-687ff969f6c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "416" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560083} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecdb53e7-6fb3-56ce-9980-4f88e189d119" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c6fa7469-cadf-5bb3-8dec-3f881cb31af1" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=1$, $x=3$, $y=1$, $y=3$, $z=2$, $z=4$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F={e}^{z}\\,i+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+4{x}^{2}yz\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{x}^{2}yz) \\\\  & =0+2 x^{2} y+4 x^{2} y \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=1}^{x=3}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=3}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & =(27-1)\\cdot (9-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =416.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7866416-74af-5891-b8c9-f6c1a3a751ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63c318c6-6247-51e3-89f5-9e01e2e02c28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{190}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560082} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b23a3e-7c17-526a-928a-85fad0743c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-190" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560105} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd986c9-62eb-5305-bc07-9934063ce422" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{76}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 1759