{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{2}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=2}^{x=3}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=2}^{y=3}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & =(27-8)\\cdot (9-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =190.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560121 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7866416-74af-5891-b8c9-f6c1a3a751ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c29a741-00a0-515e-911a-eeee07458659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560079} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4c8cc6-0565-52b9-b9f7-f6addd5c4f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560087} {:answer/id #uuid "c14d9583-f641-5ba8-a269-37856b6aa647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560101} {:answer/id #uuid "e80972f0-e878-59aa-825c-1374c6505972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560114} {:answer/id #uuid "eddb07c6-dc79-58ec-b504-1a50cd4dcb17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c29a741-00a0-515e-911a-eeee07458659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560079} :answer-field/id #uuid "e367539d-d01a-537d-bede-325402aa1114" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5492797-50b7-5ddf-a85b-d01aab96103c" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0$, $x=4$, $y=0$, $y=3$, $z=0$, $z=2$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=(7x+1)\\,i+3z\\,j+xy\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(7 x + 1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =7+0+0 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}7\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}7\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}7\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[7x]_{x=0}^{x=4}\\cdot (3-0)\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(28-0)\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =168.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7866416-74af-5891-b8c9-f6c1a3a751ac" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f64c501-23ad-5895-bb85-cd421ce0e391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560063} {:answer/id #uuid "2b4b73ce-7f0f-5fcd-afe5-4c852f86ffec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560065} {:answer/id #uuid "4f85cd44-af17-57ec-b3e1-4a6bfc979738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560075} {:answer/id #uuid "7a3d8850-b97a-5c6c-9fc9-5e352cc63c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560085} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcca4b7-8539-5240-929a-cb57e96a526b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a3d8850-b97a-5c6c-9fc9-5e352cc63c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560085} :answer-field/id #uuid "a368137c-3c2a-5f3a-bc0b-411f8e37fd7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb1a5424-5e52-51f6-a33b-f2eedeb4f7d7" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0$, $x=2$, $y=0$, $y=4$, $z=0$, $z=5$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=(8x+1)\\,i+3z\\,j+xy\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8 x + 1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =8+0+0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}8\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5}8\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{5}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[8x]_{x=0}^{x=2}\\cdot (4-0)\\cdot (5-0) \\\\  & =(16-0)\\cdot 4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =320.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Flux Across a Closed Surface"}]}
